Trivial but honestly so, and faithful to what the display says. TEX 258-260 is the equality chain "J_t(x) \;=\; f(x)\,p_t(x) -  eta^{-1}
abla p_t(x) \;=\; -\,
abla E(x)\,p_t(x) \;-\;  eta^{-1}
abla p_t(x)."; LEAN 1667-1670 proves exactly that chain under (hf : f x = -gradE x) by "rw [hf, smul_neg]", in an arbitrary real normed space. The note states plainly 'The display asserts one substitution ... that is all it says', so nothing is oversold. Worth keeping in view: the prose claim that Fokker-Planck 'specialises ... as a conservation law \partial_t p_t = -
abla_x\cdot J_t carrying the probability current' is not this lemma; it is carried by ch02_sm_langevin_fokkerplanck_nd under eq:sm-langevin.
